Source: https://github.com/MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource branch ziyi-s-oss
  commit 24856283d18328b8473cd10991c15749b88d7bf9 (branch tip, fetched 2026-11-27)
  drivers/thermal/mi_thermal_interface.c
  The thermal_max_brightness node is from
  https://github.com/MiCode/MTK_kernel_device_modules branch malachite-u-oss
  commit 36e0d9261ece65534f2ee18509b43f0bbfda0ab5,
  drivers/thermal/xiaomi/mi_thermal_interface.c.
Licence: GPL-2.0 (MODULE_LICENSE("GPL v2"), Xiaomi GPL kernel source release).
Author: "Xiaomi thermal team".

Why ziyi-s-oss: among MiCode's Qualcomm releases of this driver (zeus, ziyi,
taoyao, sky, topaz) it is the closest to stock amethyst: it uses the Qualcomm
panel_event_notifier (stock depends=panel_event_notifier,qti_battery_charger)
and has the most nodes. No 6.1 Qualcomm release of it exists in MiCode.
The MediaTek copies (malachite-u-oss, lapis-v-oss) use mtk_charger and MTK
display notifiers.

Changes:
- 6.1/clang build: include paths for base.h and thermal_core.h are set in
  Kbuild. Missing (void) prototypes and an implicit int are fixed, and printk
  formats corrected (%pOF, %ld).
- CONFIG_MI_THERMAL_MULTI_CHARGE is enabled in Kbuild. Stock has charger_temp,
  usb_online and usb_online_work.
- modem_rate is removed: stock has no such node.
- Added the nodes that the stock module has and ziyi does not:
  thermal_max_brightness (from malachite), display_therm_temp, boot_complete,
  ntn_limit, voice_limit, torch_level, torch_real_level, and the power_save
  device (/sys/class/thermal/power_save/{powersave_mode,power_level}).
  The stock module's relocations show that each of their show/store
  functions calls only snprintf/simple_strtol, so they are plain integer
  slots. Their names were checked against the stock dev_attr_* symbols.
- sconfig and board_sensor_temp stores now call
  charger_notifier_call_chain(THERMAL_SCENE / THERMAL_BOARD_TEMP, value).
  Stock calls charger_notifier_call_chain from exactly these two store
  functions, per relocations. The events and their meaning are defined by
  the in-tree consumer, drivers/power/supply/qti_battery_charger.c
  (charger_notifier handler -> XM_PROP_THERMAL_SCENE / _BOARD_TEMP to ADSP).

Result: the built module's function list, dev_attr_* list, modinfo author,
description, licence and depends are identical to the stock module's.
No decompiled code was used. The stock module was used only for symbol
names, relocation targets and strings.
